-- title:
--   Identity-component finite part lies inside the Néron finite part
-- statement:
--   Fix natural numbers $N_0$ and $p$ with $N_0 \neq 0$ and $p$ a nonzero prime, and a hypothesis $h_{pN_0}$ that $p \nmid N_0$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with `A.LiesOverPrime p`, i.e. the image of $p$ in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is a non-unit of $A$, let $\Lambda$ be level data of type `JZeroNeronObjectAtP.LevelData N₀ p A` (a structure morphism $\sigma_A : \operatorname{Spec} A \to$ `base p` lifting the generic point, a relative group law over `base p`, and identifications of the generic and special fibre point sets with $J_0(N_0)$-level data), and let $O$ be a term of `JZeroNeronObjectAtP N₀ p hpN₀ A hA Λ`, so a smooth separated group scheme $g : G \to$ `base p` together with an identification `O.pts` of `JZero (N₀ * p)` with its generic sections and the further bundled properties of that structure. Let $F$ be a `NeronExtension` of $O$: a group scheme $g_N$ over `shBase A` with the Néron model property bundle, an open immersion `F.openImm` of the base change of $O$ into it, and a specialisation map onto the component group. Then for every natural number $m$ the additive subgroup `O.finPts m` of `JZero (N₀ * p)` — generated by the $m$-torsion points $x$ for which `ExtendsToPlace A Λ.σA (O.pts x)` holds, i.e. the generic section `O.pts x` is the restriction along `barPt A` of a section of $O.g$ over $\sigma_A$ — is contained in `F.finPts m`, the subgroup generated by the $m$-torsion points $x$ satisfying `F.ExtN x`, i.e. whose image in $F$ extends to a section over `shPt A`.
--
--   This is the comparison of the two notions of "finite part" attached to $J_0(N_0p)$ at a place above $p$: points whose sections extend over $\operatorname{Spec} A$ inside the given model extend a fortiori inside the Néron extension. It is used downstream in the construction of the specialisation map on $m$-torsion and its compatibility with the group law and with Hecke operators, in the comparison of finite-flat realisations of subgroups of $J_0(N_0p)[p]$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_JZeroNeronObjectAtP_NeronExtension_finPts_le_finPts.lean

